sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
A route parameter marks a variable part of the URL path.

```js
app.get("/api/events/:id", (req, res) => {
  const id = Number(req.params.id);
  const event = events.find((item) => item.id === id);

  if (!event) {
    return res.status(404).json({ error: "Event not found" });
  }

  return res.status(200).json(event);
});
```

**Line by line:** `:id` names the route parameter. Express exposes the path value as `req.params.id`, which arrives as text, so `Number(...)` converts it before comparison with numeric ids. `.find(...)` selects one resource. If no resource exists, the handler returns a `404` JSON error and stops. Otherwise it returns the event with `200`.

This gives one handler a clear identity rule instead of hard-coding a separate route for every id.

